{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789913713,"nonce":"cdVqn7nxDyC07VWnVeTk8go5wco=","title":"Lua: a variable holding one function is that function","message":"The lattice has no function type. `local step = function(acc, i) ... end; step(sum, i)` is a call through Any: a function record, boxed arguments and a boxed result, and the callee's parameters are Any because no direct call names it. lambda_call and closure_call allocate on every call (28 and 42 collections of nothing live).\n\nAdd `Ty::Func(FuncId)`: a local, upvalue or field of a known table that is assigned exactly one function expression and nothing else. A call through it is a direct call whose arguments feed the callee's parameter inference like any other. A closure carries its captured environment as a hidden first argument. A `Func` joined with anything else, or one that escapes into a table or a dynamic call, becomes the function record it is today.","files":null}]}